      "content": "thanks, that's more like it. i was thinking about how some people say that even though those groups did amazing things, the \"real\" foundations of the modern world—like the actual institutions and the way we do science today—are still fundamentally Western. like, do you think the non-Western stuff was just \"contributions\" to a Western framework, or was it actually equal in terms of creating the structure of modern society?",
